  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Casting Wildwood Scourge for X=1 creates a fragile 1/1 that's vulnerable to almost any removal. While there's synergy with Trufflesnout next turn, the Scourge's value scales with X and with surviving to accumulate counters. A 1/1 is much easier to kill than a larger version cast later.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Wildwood Scourge for X=1, making a 1/1 Hydra",
      "betterLine": "Hold the Scourge and pass with 2 mana open. Next turn play Thriving Grove, cast Trufflesnout (choosing +1/+1 counter mode). On a later turn, cast Scourge for X=2+ when it's harder to remove and the board has more +1/+1 counter synergies established.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 22,
      "player": "GPT53C Trash",
      "decisionIndex": 12
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Casting Curiosity on the opponent's Wildwood Scourge gives the opponent card draw whenever their creature deals damage to QwCdr Folksy. This is actively harmful — it's enchanting an enemy creature with a beneficial aura. Curiosity triggers when the enchanted creature deals damage to an opponent, and from the Scourge's perspective, QwCdr Folksy is the opponent. So whenever the Scourge hits QwCdr Folksy, GPT53C Trash draws a card. This wastes a card and actively helps the opponent.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Curiosity targeting opponent's Wildwood Scourge",
      "betterLine": "Cast Narcolepsy on the opponent's Wildwood Scourge to lock it down, or simply pass and hold mana for Last Gasp as removal. Curiosity should only be cast on your own creatures.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 34,
      "player": "QwCdr Folksy",
      "decisionIndex": 15
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose Armorcraft Judge (3/3, draws 1 card) over Fertilid when Primeval Bounty ({5}{G}) is in hand. Fertilid would ramp toward the game-winning 6-mana enchantment by fetching lands, potentially casting it 1-2 turns sooner. The single card draw from Armorcraft Judge doesn't compensate for the tempo loss of delaying Primeval Bounty.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Armorcraft Judge, drawing 1 card off Trufflesnout's counter",
      "betterLine": "Cast Fertilid ({2}{G}), leaving 1 mana open. Next turn activate Fertilid to fetch a land, reaching 5 lands. Then cast Primeval Bounty on turn 6 lands instead of having to wait longer without ramp.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 109,
      "player": "GPT53C Trash",
      "decisionIndex": 43
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "At 11 life facing two 3/3 creatures with all lands untapped, the player passed their entire precombat main phase without casting any of three available spells. They had 3 mana available (UUB) and could cast Library Larcenist, Silversmote Ghoul, or Rousing Read. This wastes an entire turn of mana while significantly behind on board.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority in precombat main phase, casting nothing and effectively ending the turn.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Silversmote Ghoul (3/1 body that synergizes with Blood Artist's life gain for recursion and provides a meaningful blocker/attacker) or Library Larcenist (card draw engine). Either play develops the board when desperately behind at 11 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 135,
      "player": "QwCdr Folksy",
      "decisionIndex": 49
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Silversmote Ghoul is a fragile 3/1 with a recursion ability that's unlikely to trigger (no reliable way to gain 3 life). Meanwhile, Rousing Read on Blood Artist would immediately draw 2 cards (discard 1), create a 1/2 flyer, and provide immediate card advantage at a critical low-life juncture where finding answers matters most.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Silversmote Ghoul, deploying a fragile 3/1 with no synergy on board",
      "betterLine": "Cast Rousing Read targeting Blood Artist to immediately draw 2 cards (discard 1), create a flying blocker/threat, and dig for answers while at 11 life facing two 3/3s",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 139,
      "player": "QwCdr Folksy",
      "decisionIndex": 51
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Time to Feed before playing Forest from hand. Playing the land first is strictly better sequencing - it doesn't change available mana for this spell but ensures the land drop isn't accidentally missed and keeps options open.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Time to Feed before playing Forest land drop",
      "betterLine": "Play Forest first, then cast Time to Feed. Land drops should come before spells when there's no reason to delay them.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 147,
      "player": "GPT53C Trash",
      "decisionIndex": 55
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Blood Artist's death trigger requires choosing a target player who loses 1 life while the controller gains 1 life. QwCdr Folksy targeted themselves, meaning they lose 1 life and gain 1 life (net zero), instead of targeting the opponent for a 2-life swing (opponent loses 1, they gain 1). At 11 life against a 20 life opponent, every point matters.",
      "actionTaken": "Targeted themselves with Blood Artist's trigger, netting 0 life change.",
      "betterLine": "Target GPT53C Trash with Blood Artist's trigger so the opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life, a 2-point life swing in your favor.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 155,
      "player": "QwCdr Folksy",
      "decisionIndex": 57
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 5 life with 5 mana available, the player cast only Erratic Visionary (2 mana) instead of casting Rousing Read on Silversmote Ghoul first (3 mana, making it a 4/2 flyer and drawing 2 cards) and then casting Erratic Visionary with the remaining 2 mana. This missed both significant card advantage (draw 2) and creating a 4/2 flying threat that could attack over the opponent's ground creatures while the opponent's board was tapped.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Erratic Visionary for {1}{U}, leaving 3 mana unused and missing the opportunity to also cast Rousing Read.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Rousing Read on Silversmote Ghoul first ({2}{U}), drawing 2 cards and creating a 4/2 flyer, then cast Erratic Visionary with the remaining {1}{U}. This maximizes mana usage, card advantage, and creates a flying clock while the opponent has no flyers and Crushing Canopy is in the graveyard.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshotIndex": 178,
      "player": "QwCdr Folksy",
      "decisionIndex": 68
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
